ction.add(\n","            ids=[str(i)],\n","            documents=[sentence],\n","            embeddings=[embedding],\n","            metadatas=[metadata]\n","        )\n","\n","    print(\"All sentences successfully stored in ChromaDB!\")\n","\n","finally:\n","    client.close()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a73416e5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010053,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.650986+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.640933+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Retrieve Embeddings\n","\n","Now let's retrieve the stored vectors."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":17,"id":"cae4af2c","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.673409Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.673037Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.719447Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.71826Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.060243,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.721604+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.661361+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["ID                                     | Sentence                            | Embedding                                     | Metadata\n","------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n","0          | I love machine learning             | [-0.04363631 -0.0590543   0.08201234 -0.01076717  0.0611959 ] ... [ 0.10032279  0.06195568  0.09771024  0.01688083 -0.09040587] | {'page': 1, 'source': 'document.pdf', 'category': 'AI'}\n","1          | I enjoy coding                      | [-0.05627798 -0.03124129 -0.03912254  0.01142177  0.03994456] ... [ 0.10028355  0.02995748  0.08396302  0.00678    -0.05171905] | {'source': 'document.pdf', 'category': 'AI', 'page': 2}\n","2          | I like eating pizza                 | [-0.06539407  0.01154024  0.00051851  0.10881377 -0.09285428] ... [ 0.04528106  0.06465604  0.09007934  0.02154538 -0.08354521] | {'source': 'document.pdf', 'category': 'AI', 'page': 3}\n"]}],"source":["# Connect to database\n","client = chromadb.PersistentClient(\n","    path=\"/kaggle/working/chroma_db\"\n",")\n","\n","# Get collection\n","collection = client.get_collection(\n","    name=\"sentences\"\n",")\n","\n","# Fetch all records\n","results = collection.get(\n","    include=[\"documents\", \"embeddings\", \"metadatas\"]\n",")\n","\n","print(f\"{'ID':<38} | {'Sentence':<35} | {'Embedding':<45} | {'Metadata'}\")\n","print(\"-\" * 150)\n","\n","for i in range(len(results[\"ids\"])):\n","\n","    record_id = results[\"ids\"][i]\n","    sentence = results[\"documents\"][i]\n","    embedding = results[\"embeddings\"][i]\n","    metadata = results[\"metadatas\"][i]\n","\n","    # Display first and last 5 dimensions\n","    embedding_display = f\"{embedding[:5]} ... {embedding[-5:]}\"\n","\n","    print(\n","        f\"{record_id:<10} | \"\n","        f\"{sentence:<35} | \"\n","        f\"{str(embedding_display):<45} | \"\n","        f\"{metadata}\"\n","    )"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"c9a39f2e","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010255,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.742365+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.73211+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Production Database\n","\n","SQLite is fine for learning, but production semantic search systems commonly use vector databases.\n","\n","| Database              | Purpose                                |\n","| --------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n","| SQLite                | Basic embedding storage                |\n","| PostgreSQL + pgvector | Relational database with vector search |\n","| FAISS                 | Fast similarity search                 |\n","| ChromaDB              | Developer-friendly vector database     |\n","| Pinecone              | Managed vector database                |\n","\n","\n","## Popular vector databases\n","\n","There are several vector database technologies. You should understand their differences before choosing one for a project.\n","\n","### 1. Pinecone\n","\n","A managed cloud vector database. You don't need to manage the underlying database infrastructure yourself.\n","\n","- Managed infrastructure.\n","- Similarity search.\n","- Metadata filtering.\n","- Production RAG applications.\n","\n","Best suited to: Teams wanting managed vector infrastructure.\n","\n","[Official website](https://www.pinecone.io/)\n","\n","### 2. Qdrant\n","\n","An open-source vector database with cloud-hosted options.\n","\n","- HNSW-based vector search.\n","- Payload/metadata filtering.\n","- Quantization.\n","- Dense and sparse vector support.\n","\n","Best suited to: Production semantic search and RAG.\n","\n","[Official website](https://qdrant.tech/)\n","\n","### 3. Milvus\n","\n","A vector database designed for large-scale vector search.\n","\n","- Multiple indexing algorithms.\n","- Distributed architecture.\n","- High-dimensional vector search.\n","- Large-scale workloads.\n","\n","Best suited to: Large-scale vector retrieval.\n","\n","[Official website](https://milvus.io/)\n","\n","### 4. Weaviate\n","\n","An open-source vector database with integrated AI-oriented capabilities.\n","\n","- Semantic search.\n","- Hybrid search.\n","- Metadata filtering.\n","- Vectorization integrations.\n","\n","Best suited to: AI applications requiring flexible search.\n","\n","[Official website](https://weaviate.io/)\n","\n","### 5. Chroma\n","\n","A developer-friendly vector database often used for prototyping and RAG projects.\n","\n","- Simple Python API.\n","- Local persistence.\n","- Metadata filtering.\n","- Embedding integrations.\n","\n","Best suited to: Learning, prototyping, and smaller applications.\n","\n","[Official website](https://www.trychroma.com/)\n","\n","### 6. FAISS\n","\n","A vector similarity search library developed by Meta AI.\n","\n","- Flat search.\n","- IVF.\n","- PQ.\n","- HNSW-related indexes.\n","- CPU and GPU capabilities for supported indexes.\n","\n","Best suited to: Building custom similarity search systems and experimenting with indexing.\n","\n","[Official documentation](https://faiss.ai/)\n","\n","# Architecture of Vector Database\n","\n","This is one of the most important concepts for AI engineering interviews.\n","\n","There are two main processes:\n","\n","- Ingestion: inserting and indexing vectors.\n","- Retrieval: searching for similar vectors.\n","\n","![Vector Database Architecture](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/vector-database-architecture.png)\n","\n","## Ingestion process\n","\n","Suppose you have 100,000 PDF documents.\n","\n","You want to make them searchable using semantic search.\n","\n","The workflow is:\n","\n","1. Collect documents\n","\n","    - PDF files\n","    - Word documents\n","    - Text files\n","    - HTML pages\n","\n","2. Extract text: Extract the text from the documents.\n","\n","3. Chunk the text: Large documents are divided into smaller chunks.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","```\n","Document:\n","\"Machine learning is a field of AI.\n","It allows computers to learn from data.\n","Deep learning uses neural networks...\"\n","```\n","\n","After chunking:\n","\n","```\n","Chunk 1:\n","\"Machine learning is a field of AI.\"\n","\n","Chunk 2:\n","\"It allows computers to learn from data.\"\n","\n","Chunk 3:\n","\"Deep learning uses neural networks.\"\n","```\n","\n","4. Generate embeddings: Send each chunk to an embedding model.\n","\n","5. Store the embeddings: Store the generated vectors, IDs, text, and metadata in the vector database.\n","\n","6. Build an index: The database creates an index that helps find similar vectors without comparing every vector individually.\n","\n","We'll discuss indexing algorithms in detail below.\n","\n","## Retrieval process\n","\n","Now suppose the user asks:\n","\n","> How does machine learning work?\n","\n","The workflow is:\n","\n","1. Receive the user's query.\n","2. Convert the query into an embedding using the same compatible embedding model.\n","3. Search the vector index.\n","4. Calculate similarity between the query vector and stored vectors.\n","5. Retrieve the nearest matching records.\n","6. Return the corresponding text and metadata.\n","\n","Notice something important:\n","\n","> The vector database generally does not generate embeddings itself.\n","\n","> An external embedding model usually converts the text into vectors. Some vector database products also provide integrated embedding or inference functionality, but that is a separate capability.\n","\n","# Search Techniques\n","Search techniques are methods used to retrieve relevant documents or information from a collection based on a user's query. In vector databases and information retrieval systems, search techniques help identify the most relevant documents efficiently.\n","\n","There are two major approaches to searching:\n","\n","1. Keyword Search: Finds documents based on exact words or terms.\n","2. Semantic Search: Finds documents based on the meaning and context of the query.\n","\n","A combination of keyword search and semantic search is often used to improve search accuracy. This approach is known as Hybrid Search\n","\n","![Search Technique](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/masum184e/handbook/main/static/img/ai-engineering/search-techniques.png)\n","\n","## Keyword Search vs Semantic Search\n","\n","| Feature | Keyword Search | Semantic Search |\n","| --- | --- | --- |\n","| Main approach | Term matching | Meaning matching |\n","| Data structure | Inverted index / sparse index | Dense vector index |\n","| Techniques | BM25, TF-IDF | Embeddings |\n","| Exact matching | Excellent | Not guaranteed |\n","| Synonym understanding | Limited by analyzer | Usually better |\n","| Misspellings | Depends on configuration | Sometimes more tolerant |\n","| Technical identifiers | Excellent | Can be unreliable |\n","| Computational requirements | Often relatively inexpensive | Requires embedding and vector search |\n","\n","Suppose the user searches:\n","\n","\"car\"\n","\n","Keyword search may return:\n","\n","- Car maintenance.\n","- Car insurance.\n","- Car engines.\n","\n","Semantic search may also return:\n","\n","- Automobile maintenance.\n","- Vehicle insurance.\n","- Electric vehicles.\n","\n","Keyword search focuses on matching terms, whereas semantic search focuses on conceptual similarity.\n","\n","# Keyword Search\n","\n","Keyword Search is a traditional information retrieval technique used to find documents based on the occurrence of specific words or terms in a user's query.\n","\n","From a vector database perspective, keyword search is important because not every search problem is semantic. Sometimes users need exact matches rather than conceptually similar results.\n","\n","For example, suppose a database contains these documents:\n","\n","1. Introduction to Machine Learning\n","2. Deep Learning with Python\n","3. Machine Learning Algorithms\n","4. Introduction to Natural Language Processing\n","\n","If a user searches for `\"Machine Learning\"`, keyword search identifies documents containing those exact terms rather than documents that are merely semantically related.\n","\n","**How Keyword Search Works**\n","\n","Keyword search generally follows these steps:\n","\n","1. User Query: `\"Machine Learning Algorithms\"`\n","2. Text Processing: Tokenization, normalization, stop-word removal\n","3. Inverted Index Lookup: Find documents containing query terms\n","4. Relevance Scoring: Calculate BM25 or TF-IDF scores\n","5. Ranked Search Results: Return the most relevant documents\n","\n","Vector databases often combine keyword search with vector similarity search to provide more accurate retrieval.\n","\n","## TF IDF\n","\n","TF-IDF is a statistical technique used to determine how important a word is in a document relative to an entire collection of documents.\n","\n","The basic idea:\n","\n","- A word appearing frequently in a particular document is potentially important to that document.\n","- A word appearing in almost every document is less useful for distinguishing documents.\n","\n","TF-IDF has two components.\n","\n","### Term Frequency (TF)\n","\n","Term Frequency measures how frequently a term appears in a document.\n","\n","A simple formula:\n","\n","$$\n","TF(t,d)=\\frac{f_{t,d}}{|d|}\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $t$ = term.\n","- $d$ = document.\n","- $f_{t,d}$ = frequency of term in document.\n","- $|d|$ = total number of terms in the document.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","Document: \"Vector database is a database technology.\"\n","\n","The word \"database\" appears twice in a document containing seven words.\n","\n","$$\n","TF(database,d)=\\frac{2}{7}\n","$$\n","\n","### Inverse Document Frequency (IDF)\n","\n","IDF measures how rare or distinctive a term is across the document collection.\n","\n","$$\n","IDF(t)=\\log\\left(\\frac{N}{DF(t)}\\right)\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","- $N$ = total number of documents.\n","- $DF(t)$ = number of documents containing the term.\n","\n","For example:\n","\n","- Total documents = 1000.\n","- Documents containing \"database\" = 100.\n","\n","$$\n","IDF(database)=\\log(1000/100)\n","$$\n","\n","A rare term gets a higher IDF score, while a common term gets a lower score.\n","\n","### Final TF-IDF Score\n","\n","$$\n","TFIDF(t,d)=TF(t,d)\\times IDF(t)\n","$$\n","\n","A document receives a higher score for terms that occur frequently in that document but are relatively rare across the collection.\n","\n","In vector databases: TF-IDF can be used as a sparse representation of documents, where each dimension represents a vocabulary term and its value represents its importance.\n","\n","However, TF-IDF is not itself a vector similarity metric. The resulting sparse vectors can subsequently be compared using cosine similarity or other scoring methods.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"id":"d3474a59","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.764536Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.764165Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.813529Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.812387Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.063045,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.815725+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.75268+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["['coding' 'eating' 'enjoy' 'learning' 'like' 'love' 'machine' 'pizza']\n"]}],"source":["from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import TfidfVectorizer\n","\n","vectorizer = TfidfVectorizer()\n","tfidf_matrix = vectorizer.fit_transform(sentences1)\n","print(vectorizer.get_feature_names_out())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"id":"2939a874","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.839032Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.83866Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.845928Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.844889Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.0215,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.847978+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.826478+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["[[0.         0.         0.         0.57735027 0.         0.57735027\n","  0.57735027 0.        ]\n"," [0.70710678 0.         0.70710678 0.         0.         0.\n","  0.         0.        ]\n"," [0.         0.57735027 0.         0.         0.57735027 0.\n","  0.         0.57735027]]\n"]}],"source":["print(tfidf_matrix.toarray())"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"id":"6dd9ec69","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.146194,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.004479+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:14.858285+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"41aeada9","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.027033Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.026697Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.040836Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.039645Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02778,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.042828+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.015048+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["I love machine learning Score: 0.816496580927726\n","I like eating pizza Score: 0.0\n","I enjoy coding Score: 0.0\n"]}],"source":["query = [\"Machine Learning\"]\n","\n","# Convert query into TF-IDF vector\n","query_vector = vectorizer.transform(query)\n","\n","# Calculate cosine similarity\n","similarities = cosine_similarity(\n","    query_vector,\n","    tfidf_matrix\n",")\n","\n","# Display search results\n","scores = similarities.flatten()\n","\n","ranked_indices = scores.argsort()[::-1]\n","\n","for index in ranked_indices:\n","    print(\n","        sentences1[index],\n","        \"Score:\",\n","        scores[index]\n","    )"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"368fda5f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.010603,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.063728+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.053125+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["You might wonder: If TF-IDF already calculates word importance, why do we need cosine similarity?\n","\n","Because they perform two different jobs:\n","\n","| TF-IDF | Cosine Similarity |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| Calculates word importance | Measures vector similarity |\n","| Converts text into vectors | Compares vectors |\n","| Generates numerical representations | Generates similarity scores |\n","\n","## BM25 (Best Matching 25)\n","\n","BM25 is a ranking algorithm widely used in modern search engines and hybrid retrieval systems.\n","\n","It improves upon traditional TF-IDF by considering:\n","\n","1. Term frequency.\n","2. Inverse document frequency.\n","3. Document length normalization.\n","4. Term frequency saturation.\n","\n","The BM25 formula is:\n","\n","$$\n","\\begin{aligned}\n","BM25(D,Q)=\\sum_{t\\in Q}&IDF(t)\\\\\n","&\\times\n","\\frac{f(t,D)(k_1+1)}\n","{f(t,D)+k_1(1-b+b\\frac{|D|}{avgdl})}\n","\\end{aligned}\n","$$\n","\n","Where:\n","\n","| Parameter | Meaning |\n","| --- | --- |\n","| $D$ | Document |\n","| $Q$ | Search query |\n","| $f(t,D)$ | Frequency of term in document |\n","| $IDF(t)$ | Inverse document frequency |\n","| $\\|D\\|$ | Document length |\n","| $avgdl$ | Average document length |\n","| $k_1$ | Controls term frequency saturation |\n","| $b$ | Controls document length normalization |\n","\n","Typical values are:\n","\n","- $k_1 = 1.2$ to $2.0$\n","- $b = 0.75$\n","\n","### Why BM25 is better than basic TF-IDF\n","\n","Imagine two documents:\n","\n","- D1: \"Vector database\" (2 words)\n","- D2: \"Vector database\" repeated 50 times in a long document.\n","\n","A basic term-frequency approach might give D2 an excessively high score because the query terms appear many times.\n","\n","BM25 uses term frequency saturation, meaning that repeating a term 50 times does not necessarily make the document 50 times more relevant.\n","\n","It also normalizes for document length, helping avoid unfairly favoring longer documents.\n","\n","In vector databases: BM25 is particularly useful for retrieving documents that contain exact keywords, technical terms, product names, identifiers, or specific phrases."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"69dcf4bf","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.087917Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.087521Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-01T10:11:17.591993Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-01T10:11:17.590692Z"},"papermill":{"duration":2.518943,"end_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:17.594266+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-11-01T10:11:15.075323+00:00